{"ts": "2026-11-19T01:01:00Z", "by": "model:gemini", "entity": "specimen", "id": "C244", "op": "set", "field": "story", "old": "This 1964 20 centavos coin from Mexico was struck in brass (95% copper and 5% zinc). The reverse shows the Pyramid of the Sun at Teotihuacan with the volcanoes Popocatépetl and Iztaccíhuatl behind it under a radiant Phrygian cap (cap of liberty). At the top the value 20 is divided by the cap, with the Mo mint mark beneath it; the word CENTAVOS and the 1964 date also appear on this side. The obverse displays the Mexican national arms.", "new": "This 1964 20 centavos coin from Mexico was struck in brass (95% copper and 5% zinc). The reverse shows the Pyramid of the Sun at Teotihuacan with the volcanoes Popocatépetl and Iztaccíhuatl behind it under a radiant Phrygian cap (cap of liberty). At the top the value 20 is divided by the cap, with the Mo mint mark beneath it; the word CENTAVOS and the 1964 date also appear on this side. The obverse displays the Mexican national arms.", "source": "https://en.numista.com/959 (\"Composition Brass (95% Copper, 5% Zinc) ... The value is at the top with the radiant Liberty cap in between, and the mintmark underneath.\")", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "high", "provenance": {"model": "gemini", "prompt_version": "HOMEWORK@2026-11-06", "workflow": "homework-story-check", "assignment": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261106-1", "run_id": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261106-1", "inputs": [{"file": "https://en.numista.com/959"}], "raw": "compact answer S1"}}
